.TH VIEW-APP 1 "October 2026" "View 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
view-app \- view and annotate PDFs, images, videos, text and 3D models
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B view-app
[\fIFILE\fR...]
.br
.B view-app
\fB\-\-new\-signature\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR | \fB\-\-selftest\fR [\fB\-\-no\-ui\fR]
.br
.B view-app
\fB\-\-combine\-pdf\fR [\fB\-o\fR \fIOUT.pdf\fR] \fIIMAGE\fR...
.br
.B view-app
\fB\-\-enable\-files\-integration\fR | \fB\-\-disable\-files\-integration\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
View is a macOS Preview\-style viewer for GNOME. It opens PDF documents,
images, video and audio, CSV/TSV spreadsheets, text and source code, and
STL/OBJ/PLY 3D models. Images are grouped in one window; every other file
opens in its own window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-new\-signature
Open the signature pad (touchpad on Linux, or mouse/pen/touch).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-selftest
Check that every viewer and library works and exit with status 0 or 1.
With \fB\-\-no\-ui\fR no windows are opened (no display needed).
.TP
.B \-\-combine\-pdf
Combine images into one PDF without opening a window; see
\fBview-app \-\-combine\-pdf \-\-help\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-enable\-files\-integration
For the current user, make Space in GNOME Files show previews with View
(instead of GNOME Sushi) and add a "Combine Images into PDF" Files script.
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-files\-integration
Undo \fB\-\-enable\-files\-integration\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-quicklook
Run the Quick Look D\-Bus service (started by the session bus).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/view-app/ocr-venv
Optional text recognition engine, downloaded on request.
.TP
.I ~/Pictures/Signatures
Saved signatures.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/Zdong104/View
